These restrictions exist for one reason: to keep the port from being used to pirate the game or to spread malware.
Repackaged builds or modified copies could ship the game's content to people who don't own it, or hide harmful code
behind the port's name. Keeping every release in one place lets players trust that what they download is the real,
clean builder and that it only works with a copy they bought.

GitHub's Terms of Service allow users to view and fork public repositories on GitHub. A fork made that way does not
receive any of the rights listed above: it may not be modified, redistributed, released or used outside of that
GitHub feature.

The EBOOT.PBP files the builder produces contain data from the user's own copy of the game. They are for the personal
use of the person who owns that copy and may not be shared.

